<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="AARCH64:LE:64:v8A">
<!--
    Jump thunks named after the function they jump to
    (`option thunknames on|off`, default on).

    A function whose first instruction is a direct unconditional branch is a
    jump thunk: a linker branch island, an identical-code-folding forwarder,
    an outlined tail call. Without a symbol of its own it stays
    `sub_<addr>`, and every call through it is anonymous although its target
    is named.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 environment-binding.
    kuna-console engine/kuna_thunknames.rs decodes the first instruction of
    every discovered entry and, after every other name source, renames a
    placeholder thunk `j_<target>`; a thunk to a thunk becomes `j_j_<target>`.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture. Both passes clear
    it, load thunknames_aarch64 and take the `mode fast` inventory (static AArch64 ELF; source
    thunknames_aarch64.S): release_box is named, the unnamed thunk at
    0x210130 is `b release_box`, the one at 0x210134 is `b 0x210130`, and
    drop_box / drop_two call them with bl.

    Pass 1 (`option thunknames off`) reproduces the bug: both calls render
    sub_<addr>(). Pass 2 is the shipped default.

    Assertions span the combined output of both passes.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/thunknames_aarch64</com>
  <com>mode fast</com>
  <com>option thunknames off</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function drop_box</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function drop_two</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/thunknames_aarch64</com>
  <com>mode fast</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function drop_box</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function drop_two</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="THUNKNAMES #1: off, the call through the thunk is anonymous" min="1" max="1">sub_210130\(</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="THUNKNAMES #2: off, the call through the thunk chain is anonymous" min="1" max="1">sub_210134\(</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="THUNKNAMES #3: on, the thunk is named after its target" min="1" max="1">[^_]j_release_box\(</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="THUNKNAMES #4: on, a thunk to a thunk is named after that thunk" min="1" max="1">j_j_release_box\(</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
